# Git commits: skip hooks

The user has explicitly requested that all local commits in this workspace be made without running git hooks.

- When committing locally (`git commit`), always pass `--no-verify`.
- This applies to every future commit request in this workspace, not just a one-off case.
- This does not change other git safety rules (still no force-push, no `--amend` outside the allowed cases, etc.).
